#. read once the step is done, and held on until somebody has
#: tasks/@handover/copy-config/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Arch OS is installed\n"
"\n"
"{{ARCH_OS_HOSTNAME}} is on {{ARCH_OS_DISK}} and ready to start. Everything from here on is optional."
msgstr ""

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@handover/share-config/task.yaml
msgid "Upload the answers to paste.rs"
msgstr ""

#. asked before the step runs
#: tasks/@handover/share-config/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Put these answers online now?\n"
"\n"
"Every answer from this installation goes to paste.rs, and its address comes back as a code to scan, enough to set up another machine exactly like this one. Anyone holding that address can read them. The password is not among them and was never written down anywhere."
msgstr ""

#. read once the step is done, and held on until somebody has
#: tasks/@handover/share-config/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Configuration shared\n"
"\n"
"Scan the code, or type the word at the end of the address into the online starting point of another installation."
msgstr ""

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@handover/chroot/task.yaml
msgid "Open a shell in the new system"
msgstr ""

#. asked before the step runs
#: tasks/@handover/chroot/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Open a shell inside the system that was just installed?\n"
"\n"
"Everything is still mounted, so this is a good time to look around or fix something by hand. Leave the shell with `exit`."
msgstr ""

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@handover/reboot/task.yaml
msgid "Restart into the new system"
msgstr ""

#. asked before the step runs
#: tasks/@handover/reboot/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Restart into {{ARCH_OS_HOSTNAME}} now?\n"
"\n"
"Everything is unmounted first. Remove the installation media once the screen goes blank."
msgstr ""

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@handover/unmount/task.yaml
msgid "Unmount and lock the disk"
msgstr ""

#. asked before the step runs
#: tasks/@handover/unmount/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Unmount the new system and stay in the live environment?\n"
"\n"
"Nothing is lost either way, the installation is finished. Leaving it mounted is only useful if you want to keep working on it from here."
msgstr ""

